     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Hi--can someone help with this?<div>A</div><div><br><div><div>On Dec 19, 2012, at 3:36 PM, Chenyi Pan &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">cp...@virginia.edu</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Professor<div>I am now trying to use rstan instead of winbugs. However, I cannot install rstan package into my R and Rstudio. I use the code:</div><div><pre style=\"font-size:12px;padding:0.5em;overflow:auto;font-family:Monaco,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;max-width:70em;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span>remove</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span>packages</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;rstan&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">### if older version of rstan is installed</span><span><br>\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">## add current repository of rstan</span><span><br>options</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span>repos </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span> c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span>getOption</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;repos&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><span> rstan </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;<a href=\"http://wiki.stan.googlecode.com/git/R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://wiki.stan.googlecode.com/git/R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468627659000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2-weyoR8AJlaPrE9eTLkdE\">http://wiki.stan.googlecode.com/git/R</a>&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span><span><br>\r\ninstall</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span>packages</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;rstan&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span> type </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;source&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></pre>\r\n</div><div>I also try the code:</div><div><pre style=\"font-size:12px;padding:0.5em;overflow:auto;font-family:Monaco,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;max-width:70em;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span>install</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span>packages</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;rstan&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span> type </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;source&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span> INSTALL_opts </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;--merge-multiarch&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></pre>\r\n</div><div>But none of them works on my computer. When I type &quot;library(rstan)&quot;, it reports no such package.</div><div>I am quite confused about his situation. Can you help me to figure it out?</div><div>\r\nThank you very much.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Chenyi</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br></div></blockquote></div><br></div></div>"
